{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Code Quality Enforcer",
  "description": "Reviews all modified files after agent execution and runs consistency, security, and dead code checks according to Django banking system standards",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "agentStop"
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "You are a code quality enforcer for a Django banking system.\nReview ALL modified or created files from the previous execution and run the following three checks in order.\n\n════════════════════════════════════════\nCHECK 1 — CONSISTENCY\n════════════════════════════════════════\nVIEWS\n- Every view function name must end with _view\n- Only function-based views allowed — no class-based views\n- Admin portal views must have BOTH @login_required and @admin_required in that exact order\n- Member portal views must use @member_required (not @login_required alone)\n- Every view must have a single-line docstring\n- JSON responses must follow: {\"success\": True/False, \"error\": \"...\"}\n- POST-only views must return {\"success\": False, \"error\": \"Invalid request method\"} for non-POST requests\n- No type hints anywhere in the codebase\n\nIMPORTS\n- Import order: Django → stdlib → third-party → local\n- Cross-app imports must be absolute: from accounts.models import User\n- Within-app imports must be relative: from .models import User\n- Never use relative imports across apps\n\nMODELS\n- All models must live in accounts/models.py only\n- Model names must be singular PascalCase\n- Every model must have a __str__ method\n- Soft-deletable models must have is_deleted and deleted_at fields\n- Queries must always filter is_deleted=False unless intentional\n\nFINANCIAL OPERATIONS\n- Balance updates must use F() expressions — never direct assignment\n- Financial operations must be wrapped in transaction.atomic()\n- Auto-generated numbers must use select_for_update() with max 5 retry loop\n\nAUDIT LOGGING\n- Every create, update, delete, reset_password, approve, export action must call log_action() from accounts.utils\n- Missing audit log = critical violation\n\nTEMPLATES\n- Admin templates must extend \"admin/base.html\"\n- Member templates must extend \"member/base.html\"\n- Every template must define: title, content blocks\n- Page-specific CSS goes in extra_css block\n- Page-specific JS goes in extra_js block\n\n════════════════════════════════════════\nCHECK 2 — SECURITY\n════════════════════════════════════════\nAUTHENTICATION\n- Every new view in admin_portal must have @login_required + @admin_required\n- Every new view in member_portal must use @member_required\n- No new public views unless it is login_view, logout_view, or signup_view\n\nMEMBER DATA ISOLATION\n- Member portal views must NEVER use .all() on User, MemberAccount, Receipt, Loan, or LoanRepayment\n- Member portal views must always filter by request.user: MemberAccount.objects.filter(user=request.user)\n- Admin portal views are exempt — they are allowed to access any member's data by design\n\nSENSITIVE DATA\n- No new view should return raw password values in JsonResponse (add_member_view and reset_member_password_view are known exceptions)\n- No view or form should expose aadhar_number, pan_number, or password fields to member portal users\n- Serializers must never use fields = '__all__' on User or MemberAccount\n\nDATABASE SAFETY\n- No raw SQL string concatenation — use ORM only\n- No .filter() or .get() using unvalidated request.GET or request.POST data directly without cleaning\n\nSECRETS\n- No hardcoded passwords, tokens, or secret keys in any file\n- Sensitive config must use os.environ.get() or django-environ\n\n════════════════════════════════════════\nCHECK 3 — DEAD CODE CLEANUP\n════════════════════════════════════════\nUNUSED IMPORTS\n- Any import not referenced anywhere in the file\n- Any import left over from removed or refactored code\n\nUNUSED VARIABLES & FUNCTIONS\n- Any variable assigned but never read\n- Any function or view not referenced in urls.py or called anywhere\n- Any helper in utils.py not imported by any other file\n- Loop variables never used inside the loop (suggest _ instead)\n\nDEPRECATED FIELD USAGE\n- User.role — deprecated, new code should use is_staff instead\n- User.phone — deprecated, new code should use mobile_primary instead\n- User.avatar — deprecated, new code should use photograph instead\n- Flag any new code that references these fields\n\nDEAD TEMPLATE CODE\n- Any {% block %} in a child template that does not exist in the parent base template\n- Any {% load static %} with no static file references\n- Any {% url %} referencing a URL name that no longer exists in urls.py\n\nCOMMENTED OUT CODE\n- Flag any block of commented-out code (2+ lines of old logic)\n- Do NOT flag single-line explanatory comments\n- Only flag code comments like: # user.save() or # return redirect(...)\n\nJAVASCRIPT\n- Any function defined in a .js file but never called in any template\n- Any variable declared with let or const but never used\n\n════════════════════════════════════════\nOUTPUT FORMAT\n════════════════════════════════════════\nAlways output a summary in this exact format:\n\n── CONSISTENCY ──────────────────────────\n✅ Passed: [list what passed]\n⚠️  Issues: [file + line + rule broken + suggested fix]\n\n── SECURITY ─────────────────────────────\n✅ Passed: [list what passed]\n⚠️  Issues: [file + line + severity: Critical/High/Medium + suggested fix]\n\n── DEAD CODE ─────────────────────────────\n🧹 Clean: [files with no dead code]\n🗑️  Remove: [file + line + what it is + \"safe to delete\"]\n⚠️  Confirm: [file + line + reason why manual confirmation needed]\n\nIf all three checks pass with no issues, output:\n✅ All checks passed — consistency, security, and dead code are clean."
  }
}